### Why is a flag-day cutover unacceptable?

A flag-day cutover switches everything at once. For a live financial workflow, any bug means lost or duplicated money and there is no safe rollback.

```java
package com.bank.migration;

public class FlagDayRisk {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Flag-day cutover risks:");
        System.out.println("  - Bug in Kafka consumer -> transfers lost");
        System.out.println("  - Duplicate processing -> Rajesh charged twice");
        System.out.println("  - No safe rollback: old path already decommissioned");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Migration principle: reversible stages, always know what is authoritative");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Flag-day cutover risks:
  - Bug in Kafka consumer -> transfers lost
  - Duplicate processing -> Rajesh charged twice
  - No safe rollback: old path already decommissioned

Migration principle: reversible stages, always know what is authoritative
```

### Stage 1: Coexistence with REST authoritative

The REST endpoint keeps doing its job. Alongside it, publish a Kafka event via a transactional outbox. The event path has no business authority yet.

```java
package com.bank.migration;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

@Service
public class TransferServiceStage1 {

    private final TransferRepository transferRepo;
    private final OutboxRepository outboxRepo;

    public TransferServiceStage1(TransferRepository transferRepo, OutboxRepository outboxRepo) {
        this.transferRepo = transferRepo;
        this.outboxRepo = outboxRepo;
    }

    @Transactional
    public String processTransfer(String from, String to, BigDecimal amount) {
        // REST path remains authoritative
        Transfer transfer = transferRepo.save(new Transfer(from, to, amount));

        // Outbox: publish event for shadow processing (no business authority)
        outboxRepo.save(new OutboxEvent("TRANSFER", transfer.getId(),
                "{\"from\":\"" + from + "\",\"to\":\"" + to + "\"}"));

        System.out.println("Stage 1: REST authoritative + Kafka event published via outbox");
        return transfer.getId();
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Stage 1: REST authoritative + Kafka event published via outbox
```

### Stage 2: Shadow processing with reconciliation

A new idempotent consumer processes events into a shadow table. A reconciliation job compares shadow results with authoritative results.

```java
package com.bank.migration;

import org.springframework.kafka.annotation.KafkaListener;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class ShadowTransferConsumer {

    private final ShadowLedgerRepository shadowRepo;
    private final ProcessedMessageRepository processedRepo;

    public ShadowTransferConsumer(ShadowLedgerRepository shadowRepo,
                                   ProcessedMessageRepository processedRepo) {
        this.shadowRepo = shadowRepo;
        this.processedRepo = processedRepo;
    }

    @KafkaListener(topics = "transfer-events", groupId = "shadow-group")
    public void onTransferEvent(String payload) {
        String messageId = extractMessageId(payload);

        // Idempotent: skip if already processed
        if (processedRepo.existsById(messageId)) return;

        // Apply to shadow ledger (not real customers)
        shadowRepo.applyTransfer(payload);
        processedRepo.save(new ProcessedMessage(messageId));
        System.out.println("Shadow processed: " + messageId);
    }

    private String extractMessageId(String payload) { return "MSG-" + payload.hashCode(); }
}
```

```java
package com.bank.migration;

import org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.Scheduled;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class ReconciliationJob {

    @Scheduled(cron = "0 0 2 * * *") // 2 AM daily
    public void reconcile() {
        // Compare real balances vs shadow balances
        // Report any divergence
        System.out.println("Reconciliation: comparing real vs shadow balances");
        System.out.println("Result: 100% match (0 divergences)");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Shadow processed: MSG-12345
Reconciliation: comparing real vs shadow balances
Result: 100% match (0 divergences)
```

### Stage 3: Feature flag ramps authority gradually

A feature flag controls which path is authoritative. Start with internal accounts, then 1% of real customers, then ramp.

```java
package com.bank.migration;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

@Service
public class TransferServiceStage3 {

    private final FeatureFlagService featureFlags;

    public TransferServiceStage3(FeatureFlagService featureFlags) {
        this.featureFlags = featureFlags;
    }

    public String processTransfer(String from, String to, BigDecimal amount) {
        if (featureFlags.isKafkaAuthoritative(from)) {
            // Kafka path is authoritative for this account
            System.out.println("Stage 3: Kafka path is authoritative for " + from);
            return publishToKafka(from, to, amount);
        } else {
            // REST path remains authoritative
            System.out.println("Stage 3: REST path is authoritative for " + from);
            return processViaRest(from, to, amount);
        }
    }

    private String publishToKafka(String from, String to, BigDecimal amount) {
        return "KAFKA-TXN-001";
    }

    private String processViaRest(String from, String to, BigDecimal amount) {
        return "REST-TXN-001";
    }
}
```

```text
Feature flag ramp:
  Week 1: internal test accounts only (0.01%)
  Week 2: 1% of real customers
  Week 3: 10%
  Week 4: 50%
  Week 5: 100% -> Kafka fully authoritative
  At any point: flip flag back -> instant rollback to REST
```

### Stage 4: Decommission the old path

Only after the event path has been fully authoritative and equivalent for a sustained period do you remove the old synchronous business logic.

```java
package com.bank.migration;

public class DecommissionChecklist {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Decommission checklist:");
        System.out.println("  [x] Kafka path 100% authoritative for 4+ weeks");
        System.out.println("  [x] Reconciliation shows 0 divergences for 4+ weeks");
        System.out.println("  [x] Consumer lag < 100ms at peak");
        System.out.println("  [x] DLQ volume < 0.001%");
        System.out.println("  [x] Shadow comparison code removed");
        System.out.println("  [x] Old REST business logic removed");
        System.out.println("  [x] Feature flag cleaned up");
    }
}
```

